    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78-a4">

                <pb facs="0200" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg106"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    73.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Montalvo to Mr. Tillman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I inclose to your excellency copy
                    of a telegram from Mr. Santos to the supreme chief of the Republic concerning
                    bases of arrangement of the claim of Santos, which he proposes.</p>
                <p>By said telegram you can see that the affair is under way of solution. Would that
                    the claims of Mr. Santos may be so equitable that the Government may accept them
                    opportunely. I avail myself of this opportunity to renew to your excellency the
                    assurances of my distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis J.
                    Montalvo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
